---
export const title = 'Events';
export const order = 500;
import Highlighter from '../../../../components/Highlighter.astro';
---
<p>
  <code>menu-item-activate</code> bubbles from the menu with the activated item.
  <code>open</code> and <code>close</code> fire after the menu opens and closes. Like every Peacock overlay,
  <code>close</code> carries <code>detail.reason</code>: <code>action</code> (an item was picked),
  <code>escape</code>, <code>light-dismiss</code> (a press outside, or Tab moving focus out) or
  <code>api</code> (<code>close()</code> or <code>open = false</code>). <code>detail.cause</code> keeps the
  menu's detailed reason: <code>click-selection</code>, <code>keydown</code> (with the key),
  <code>outside-click</code> or <code>programmatic</code>.
</p>
<p>
  Both events bubble and cross shadow roots, so a submenu's events reach a listener on its parent menu.
  Check <code>event.target</code> to handle only the menu's own.
</p>
<Highlighter lang={'javascript'} is:raw>const menu = document.querySelector('wc-menu');

menu.addEventListener('menu-item-activate', event => {
  console.log('Activated', event.detail.item.value);
});

menu.addEventListener('close', event => {
  if (event.target !== menu) return;
  console.log('Closed by', event.detail.reason, event.detail.cause.kind);
});</Highlighter>

<h3>Deprecated</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    <code>opened</code> and <code>closed</code>: use <code>open</code> and <code>close</code>. They still fire
    on the menu itself without bubbling, and <code>closed</code> still carries the menu reason as
    <code>detail.reason</code>.
  </li>
</ul>
